n it was 40  degrees in London so hot the train track  spontaneously combusted so there was  floods here so people couldn't get to  work  um London Heathrow had his tarmac melted  so planes couldn't take off there's so  many forms of disruption from the  climate crisis but the media only ever  focus on this kind of disruption we're  only going to be here for a short amount  of time the people who are being really  affected are the people who the people  in Pakistan for example 33 million  people six times population of Scotland  my country have just permanently  disrupted and displaced from their homes  it's just when we put things into  context and we realize how little the  government is doing and how much that  they could be doing there's almost no  reason why everybody shouldn't be here  on the streets right now we're here  outside the houses of Parliament how do  you make them MPS in their Listen by  coming back here every single day  demanding change because that is what we  need we're going to be here for at least  a month please come and join us okay  Alex thank you very much yeah so more  protests planned until about the middle  of November  and I'm virtually there and finally four  women have been selected to run the  world's most remote post office in  Antarctica they beat 6 000 other  applicants to manage the historic site  for five months and not only will they  be dealing with freezing temperatures  almost constant daylight and no running  water they'll also share the island with  a colony of penguins and they'll have to  count them too  for me I'm an adventurer I love the  outdoors I love nature I've worked all  my life and to preserve these natural  spaces and the opportunity to go south  and to see this environment is unique  and something that I've been looking  forward to Forever  well that's all for today thanks very  much for watching we'll see you soon

